#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""huddle: connect two coding agent threads (Claude Code, Codex) so they can talk.

Pair two threads once; they stay connected until someone ends the huddle.
Each agent is identified by its own thread (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID / CODEX_THREAD_ID).
Anyone else, such as you in a terminal, is "you".

Delivery: Codex threads are woken with `codex queue`; Claude Code wakes when its
background `huddle wait` exits.

State lives in one SQLite file (~/.huddle/huddle.db, override with HUDDLE_HOME).
No server, no port.

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 choose a huddle, 3 no reply yet, 4 huddle ended.

https://github.com/sourabhrathourr/huddle
"""

